# What belongs in this repository: the harness, the experiment definition, and
# the record of what was run. Not the game binaries, not the recordings, and
# not anything a script can rebuild.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Derived. Delete any of this and `python app/export.py --rebuild` puts it back.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
analysis/
sensors/data/processed/

# Rendered from FPSci/scripts/analysis/guide.html by build_guide.py.
FPSci-Aim-Training-Guide.pdf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Raw recordings. Roughly 12 MB per run and gigabytes over a study, so they do
# not belong in git -- but they are also irreplaceable, so BACK THEM UP
# somewhere else. Nothing here can regenerate them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
FPSci-bin/results/
sensors/data/raw/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The FPSci distribution: ~174 MB of vendor executable, DLLs and assets. The
# config files next to them are ours and are the experiment definition, so
# those are pulled back in below.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
FPSci-bin/*
!FPSci-bin/experimentconfig.Any
!FPSci-bin/startupconfig.Any
!FPSci-bin/keymap.Any
!FPSci-bin/systemconfig.Any

# Regenerated by app/run_study.py on every launch, and userstatus.Any is
# rewritten by FPSci itself at the end of every session. Tracking them would be
# a stream of meaningless diffs.
FPSci-bin/userstatus.Any
FPSci-bin/userconfig.Any
FPSci-bin/userstatus.sessions.csv
FPSci-bin/log.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Upstream FPSci checkout. It carries its own .git, so tracking it here would
# create a stray gitlink; clone it separately instead.
#
# NOTE: FPSci/scripts/analysis/ is NOT part of upstream -- it is untracked in
# that repository too. See the note in app/README.md before deleting or
# re-cloning FPSci/.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
FPSci/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and OS clutter
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*~
*.bak

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT ignored:
#
#   study/sittings.csv   which warm-up condition was running, and when. It is
#                        written by the launcher, cannot be derived from the
#                        databases, and was destroyed once already. Small, and
#                        exactly what version control is for.
#
#   docs/config-before-rewrite/   the config that produced the pilot data.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
